# Response headers for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages, which read this file from the published
# folder: `npx expo export` copies it there from public/. Apache: public/.htaccess. nginx:
# deploy/nginx.conf. The three carry the same values. The pages carry the same
# Content-Security-Policy as a <meta> tag (less frame-ancestors, which a meta tag cannot set) for
# a host that sends no headers of its own, such as GitHub Pages: 404.html as written, and
# index.html as scripts/build-web.mjs writes it from the `/*` rule below.
# __tests__/website.test.ts holds every copy equal, and e2e/run.mjs plays the game under this file.
#
# Content-Security-Policy, measured in Chromium with the game played end to end and the policy
# sent as a response header:
#   script-src 'self'   the bundle and guard.js; Expo's single-page export writes no inline script.
#   style-src 'self' 'sha256-47DEQ...'   site.css, and the empty <style> element react-native-web
#                       creates and then fills through the CSSOM (insertRule), which CSP does not
#                       govern. The hash is the empty string's: without it the game draws with no
#                       styles at all. No 'unsafe-inline'.
#   img-src 'self'      the favicon. The boards and hulls are drawn from views, not images.
#   connect-src 'none'  the game makes no network request: there is no network code.
#   frame-ancestors 'none'   nothing is meant to frame the game (clickjacking).
#   require-trusted-types-for 'script'; trusted-types 'none'   nothing writes HTML from a string.
#   No font-src, media-src, worker-src or manifest-src: the game uses the platform's own fonts,
#   plays no sound, starts no worker and does not install, so default-src 'none' refuses them.
# Referrer-Policy: no address in the game carries anything private (one page, no query, no
# share link), so a link out says which site it came from and nothing more.
# Permissions-Policy turns off every feature Chromium knows that a page can ask for: the game
# uses none of them (a browser cannot vibrate for it; src/ui/feedback.ts sends nothing on the
# web). Names Chromium does not recognise are left out, since each is a console warning.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'sha256-47DEQpj8HBSa+/TImW+5JCeuQeRkm5NMpJWZG3hSuFU='; img-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests; require-trusted-types-for 'script'; trusted-types 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), attribution-reporting=(), autoplay=(), browsing-topics=(), camera=(), clipboard-read=(), clipboard-write=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(), gamepad=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), identity-credentials-get=(), idle-detection=(), join-ad-interest-group=(), local-fonts=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), otp-credentials=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), private-aggregation=(), publickey-credentials-create=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), run-ad-auction=(), screen-wake-lock=(), serial=(), shared-storage=(), shared-storage-select-url=(), storage-access=(), usb=(), window-management=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Cache lifetimes. The bundle carries a hash of its contents in its name, so it can be kept a
# year; everything else keeps its name from one deploy to the next and is revalidated on every
# load. No path matches two of these rules: both hosts join a header that two matching rules set
# into one comma-separated value.
/_expo/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/404.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/guard.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/site.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/.well-known/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
